 },
 "summary": "A surface-mount bandpass filter for 50 Ω systems with a passband of 2170 to 2380 MHz around a 2275 MHz centre. It is built from 12 layers of low-temperature co-fired ceramic in a 3.2 mm by 1.6 mm FV1206 case with wrap-around terminations. Passband insertion loss is 3.0 dB at most (about 2 dB typical); rejection is typically 20 dB below 1720 MHz and 25 dB from 4200 to 6000 MHz. Uses named for it are harmonic rejection in transmitters and receivers.",
