 "circuits": [],
 "equations": [],
 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Construction",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Twelve layers of low-temperature co-fired ceramic (LTCC) make up the filter, which keeps it small and its response repeatable from part to part. Its terminations wrap around the body ends, which limits parasitic variation, solders well and leaves the joints visible for inspection. The part is hermetically sealed and temperature stable, and its LTCC body suits high humidity and wide temperature swings."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Frequency response",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The response is defined by five frequencies: F1 to F2 (2170 to 2380 MHz) is the passband, DC to F3 (1720 MHz) the lower stopband, and F4 to F5 (4200 to 6000 MHz) the upper stopband. Sharp rejection peaks sit just outside the passband edges, and further peaks fall at harmonic frequencies; the typical loss reaches about 49 dB near 1540 MHz and about 60 dB near 4900 MHz."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Functional schematic",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Between RF IN and RF OUT the signal passes a series capacitor and a series inductor at each port; each of the two inner nodes is shunted to ground by an inductor and a capacitor in parallel, with further sections between those nodes."
  },
  {
   "topic": "DC on the ports",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The filter is not to be used as a DC block. A port that carries DC needs its own blocking capacitor."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Land pattern",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Suggested land pattern: two end pads 1.80 mm (P, max) long, 2.21 mm (H) apart on the inside and 4.29 mm (G) across the outside; two ground pads 0.61 mm (J) wide, 0.61 mm (L) apart and 3.10 mm (K) across, each with a 0.30 mm (N) plated through-hole, the two holes 2.21 mm (M) apart. Tolerance ±.002."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Demo board",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Test board TB-270 uses layout PL-137: coplanar waveguide with a .038 in trace and .013 in gaps on Rogers RO4350B .020 in ±.0015 in thick, 1/2 oz copper each side, and a continuous ground plane on the bottom. It has eight .015 in plated through-holes. Further layout dimensions: .098, .072 (typ), .021 (typ), .028 (typ), .024 (typ) and .019 in (2 places). On another laminate the trace width and gap may need to change. The top copper is covered by SMOBC solder mask except at the land pattern."
  }
 ],
